caption: Shared Psi level caps
engine-rule: shared-psi-level-caps

Enhanced Defenses are a shared exception: Enhanced Dodge, Enhanced Parry, and Enhanced Block are each capped at ceil(governing Psi Talent or Talent-equivalent / 2) levels. This replaces the ordinary Buff or low-base-cost leveled-trait cap for those traits and is not doubled by Master Psionic. A stricter Domain, Tradition, ability, or bespoke restricted-defense cap controls.

Innate Attack damage is capped at Talent × 2 dice. Binding is capped at Talent × 4 levels. Affliction is capped at Talent levels.

A Buff is a leveled trait that increases a primary attribute, secondary attribute, or Damage Resistance. Buffs are capped at (Talent × 2) - 1 without Master Psionic and Talent × 2 with Master Psionic.

A non-attack, non-Buff leveled trait with an unmodified base cost of 25 points or less per level uses the Buff cap. A higher-base-cost leveled trait is capped at Talent.

Telekinesis, Create, Control, Temperature Control, Binding, and Penetrating Vision use the campaign-wide exceptional level caps in GATES Enhancement Limitations when those Advantages are otherwise legal. Psi Basic-access Telekinesis retains its stricter Basic cap; Advanced and Master Telekinesis use the universal Telekinesis formula.

Access band and category Mastery are separate. Tradition Mastery may grant Master access to the Tradition's Talents and abilities. Master Psionic governs applicable Talent 5+, the Will/5 Talent cap, the Psi IQ allowance, and the Mastery-dependent increase to shared level caps.

These shared Psi access and cap rules are inherited unless a Domain or Tradition explicitly changes them.
